/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/README.md:40:Lake is part of the [lean4](https://github.com/leanprover/lean4) repository and is distributed along with its official releases (e.g., as part of the [elan](https://github.com/leanprover/elan) toolchain). So if you have installed a semi-recent Lean 4 nightly, you should already have it! If you want to build the latest version from the source yourself, check out the [build instructions](#building-and-running-lake-from-the-source) at the bottom of this README.
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/README.md:44:To create a new package, either run `lake init` to setup the package in the current directory or `lake new` to create it in a new directory. For example, we could create the package `hello` like so:
