codex
The failure is caused by the audit sandbox’s PID namespace: Lean asks `/proc/<its pid>/exe`, but this container exposes only `/proc/self/exe`, so both Lean and Lake mislocate themselves. `unshare --mount-proc` is unavailable. I’m applying a narrowly scoped runtime shim that redirects only `/proc/<numeric pid>/exe` lookups to `/proc/self/exe`; it does not touch any audit input or alter Lean semantics, and I’ll preserve the shim source and probe output as evidence before rerunning preflight.
apply patch
